X:1
T:Awake, My Soul, And With The Sun
T:OLD 100TH
C:Music: Genevan Psalter, attr. Louis Bourgeois, c. 1551 · Words: Thomas Ken, 1674
S:Open Hymnal Project ABC (openhymnal.org; marked public domain), melody line with every stanza as printed there; their source: ccel from Sternhold and Hopkins' Psalter 1561.. No second score was available to cross-check the melody.
M:none
L:1/4
Q:1/4=120
K:G
G2 G F E D | G2 A2 B3 | B2 B B A G | c2 B2 A3 |
w: A- wake, my soul, and with the sun Thy dail- y stage of du- ty run;
w: Thy prec- ious time mis- spent, re- deem, Each pre- sent day thy last es- teem,
w: By in- flu- ence of Light di- vine Let thy own light to o- thers shine.
w: In con- ver- sa- tion be sin- cere; Keep con- science as the noon- tide clear;
w: Wake, and lift up thy- self, my heart, And with the an- gels bear thy part,
G2 A B A G | E2 F2 G3 | d2 B G A c | B2 A2 G3 |]
w: Shake off dull sloth, and joy- ful rise, To pay thy morn- ing sac- ri- fice.
w: Im- prove thy tal- ent with due care; For the great day thy- self pre- pare.
w: Re- flect all Heaven's pro- pit- ious ways In ar- dent love, and cheer- ful praise.
w: Think how all see- ing God thy ways And all thy sec- ret thoughts sur- veys.
w: Who all night long un- wear- ied sing High praise to the e- ter- nal King.
